This word would be useful in contexts where an implicit contrast
between two candidates for lojbanicity is intended...but often no
such comparison exists. Now, you __could__ allow ''lobykai'' to
mean ''ckaji lesi'o lojbo'' but we all know what disastrous effects
recourse to a NU-class abstractor can have! (''mi'e maikl.'')

One can also use ''lobza'a'' to ascribe lojbanicity as a virtue. --((xorxes))
(''mi nelci levi valsi'' --''mi'e maikl.'')

----

The normal usage ''lobykai'' sees is precisely equivalent to
''lojbo''.  --jrd.
